{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-fiber-domain","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0081","math_ordinal":712,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The left side is the a-superlevel set of the component function f_i.  Its domain restriction is dom f_i, not the domain of the disjoint-sum function f.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt214.tex:753","source_normalized_sha256":"3f8f51e8127b837609e066edce180f3b1e14b5bf543a7fc36bff662351ca049b","source_text":"$\\{x:(x,i)\\in F_a\\}=E_i\\cap\\dom f$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt214.tex:775","target_normalized_sha256":"258ebd592826fab17273c67d48ee1be37656af2ea53a89a663a0175e568200c2","target_text":"$\\{x:(x,i)\\in F_a\\}=E_i\\cap\\dom f_i$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S214"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-component-measure","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0082","math_ordinal":732,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Each F_nki is a subset of the component space X_i.  Both iterated-sum terms must use the component measure mu_i, consistent with the immediately following integrals against mu_i.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt214.tex:769-770","source_normalized_sha256":"22139831db5491f36aa89838dd8bd73807442c93715889ad7eea95756f153193","source_text":"two occurrences of $\\mu F_{nki}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt214.tex:793-794","target_normalized_sha256":"587e21b48404b00a4f969b9903573937c3c2cd2401f2cfe763e37a1faa1522d8","target_text":"two occurrences of $\\mu_i F_{nki}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S214"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-set-in-fiber-definition","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0083","math_ordinal":738,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The preceding sentence chooses a conegligible set E in the domain of f.  E_i must be its i-th fiber; taking a fiber of X_i is ill-typed and would not support the subsequent conegligibility identity.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt214.tex:779","source_normalized_sha256":"b16084689422bcbc7379752d8ce9f8c2da73ffb50f92ac3553eb2c8989903dc5","source_text":"$E_i=\\{x:(x,i)\\in X_i\\}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt214.tex:803","target_normalized_sha256":"d9f360db5025b5200aae925bf8be6cba9d1b751a3f94c330aca6ed0cfd4b956d","target_text":"$E_i=\\{x:(x,i)\\in E\\}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S214"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-algebra-membership","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0084","math_ordinal":828,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"This paragraph proves that Lambda is closed under countable unions.  The union F need only belong to Lambda; claiming it belongs to the original sigma-algebra Sigma is not established and is false in general.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt214.tex:859","source_normalized_sha256":"65b127545966720002875b7921f02a35d214624fcf61cbaceb81857933de3616","source_text":"$F\\in\\Sigma$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt214.tex:890","target_normalized_sha256":"c70aaa4404847c6c8d1579a37096de6fab1d7a778a5b489f3ca34c2d9c30fe7d","target_text":"$F\\in\\Lambda$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S214"}
